      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-sample/q2",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:50mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-sample/q02-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1: shape ABCDOA; a shaded sector AOB of one circle centre O on the left and a sector COD of a smaller circle centre O on the right, with angle COD = 0.4 radians, arc CD = 3 cm and AOD a straight line of length 12 cm\"></figure><p>The shape <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABCDOA\"></span>, as shown in Figure 1, consists of a sector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"COD\"></span> of a circle centre <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span> joined to a sector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AOB\"></span> of a different circle, also centre <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span>.</p><p>Given that arc length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"CD=3\\text{ cm}\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\angle COD=0.4\"></span> radians and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AOD\"></span> is a straight line of length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12\\text{ cm}\"></span>,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>find the length of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"OD\"></span>, <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>find the area of the shaded sector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AOB\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
