      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-sample/q5",
      "question": "<p>A curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has parametric equations</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=2t-1,\\qquad y=4t-7+\\frac{3}{t},\\qquad t\\neq 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>Show that the Cartesian equation of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> can be written in the form</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac{2x^2+ax+b}{x+1},\\qquad x\\neq -1\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are integers to be found. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
