      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-sample/q8",
      "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\ln(2x-5)+2x^2-30,\\qquad x&gt;2.5\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=0\"></span> has a root <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> in the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[3.5, 4]\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>A student takes 4 as the first approximation to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span>.</p><p>Given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(4)=3.099\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f&#x27;(4)=16.67\"></span> to 4 significant figures,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>apply the Newton-Raphson procedure once to obtain a second approximation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span>, giving your answer to 3 significant figures. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> is the only root of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=0\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
