    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-sample/q12",
      "question": "<p>In a controlled experiment, the number of microbes, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N\"></span>, present in a culture <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> days after the start of the experiment were counted.</p><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> are expected to satisfy a relationship of the form</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"N=aT^b,\\qquad\\text{where } a \\text{ and } b \\text{ are constants}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that this relationship can be expressed in the form<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\log_{10}N=m\\log_{10}T+c\" data-display=\"true\"></div>giving <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> in terms of the constants <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and/or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:65mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-sample/q12-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 3: graph of log10 N (0 to 5.0) against log10 T (0 to 1.4) on grid paper, with six plotted crosses and a line of best fit from about (0, 1.85) to about (1.2, 4.6)\"></figure><p>Figure 3 shows the line of best fit for values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\log_{10}N\"></span> plotted against values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\log_{10}T\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Use the information provided to estimate the number of microbes present in the culture 3 days after the start of the experiment. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Explain why the information provided could not reliably be used to estimate the day when the number of microbes in the culture first exceeds 1 000 000. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>With reference to the model, interpret the value of the constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
