      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-sample/q13",
      "question": "<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has parametric equations</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=2\\cos t,\\qquad y=\\sqrt3\\cos 2t,\\qquad 0\\leqslant t\\leqslant\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find an expression for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> lies on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}\"></span></p><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> is the normal to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Show that an equation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> is<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2x-2\\sqrt3y-1=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> intersects the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> again at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>Find the exact coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span>.<br>You must show clearly how you obtained your answers. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
