      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:60mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-sample/q15-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 5: sketch of y = f(x) starting at the origin, rising to a maximum P, falling through the x-axis to a minimum Q below it, then approaching the x-axis\"></figure><p>Figure 5 shows a sketch of the curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\"></span>, where</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac{4\\sin 2x}{\\mathrm e^{\\sqrt2x-1}},\\qquad 0\\leqslant x\\leqslant\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The curve has a maximum turning point at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> and a minimum turning point at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span> as shown in Figure 5.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> coordinates of point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> and point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span> are solutions of the equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\tan 2x=\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Using your answer to part (a), find the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-coordinate of the minimum turning point on the curve with equation<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(2x)\"></span>.</li><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3-2\\mathrm f(x)\"></span>.</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
